posts.legenda:
Stop being human cron. There’s a 3-minute setup inside Claude Code that runs your boring work while you sleep.

Type `/schedule`, write the prompt like you’d brief a teammate, pick a time, hit save once. From then on, it runs on Anthropic’s infra — every morning at 7am, every weekday at 8:55, every 2 hours — until you turn it off.

The 4 I’d build first:

@daily/inbox-triage reads my email and drafts replies in Notion before I’m awake.

@weekday/standup-prep pulls overnight commits + open PRs and posts the Slack thread so I just say “see thread.”

@daily/trend-hunter scrapes top Claude posts from X overnight and drafts 3 ready-to-shoot Reels scripts in my voice.

@hourly/bug-sentinel scans Sentry every 2 hours, groups errors by root cause, and opens Linear tickets with stack traces.

Apps need you to open them. Routines run while you sleep. Stop adding tools. Start subtracting work.

Pick the smallest thing you do every week. Ship it today. Make another tomorrow.

Comment “ROUTINES” and I’ll send the full guide with copy-paste prompts.

